call Delaware to recalculate your taxes via Assumed Par Value Method.

.why = the assessment on file was computed under § 503(a)(1), Authorized Shares,
because a report was absent — § 502(c) directs exactly that. this call confirms
the balance, the years, and the order of operations, so the reports that follow
are correct on the first submission.

> 🚩 **this `.why` read "you must call to request recalculation. this cannot be
> done online." until a later pass. it named the wrong instrument.**
>
> § 502(c) grants the election *"by **filing the annual franchise tax report**
> and complying with the provisions of § 503(b)."* the **report** is the
> instrument; the call is coordination and grants no election. a reader who
> believed the old line would end a productive call and wait for a revised bill
> that never issues.
>
> ⚠️ "this cannot be done online" is also contradicted by this route's own later
> step, which files amended reports through the tax portal at a per-year fee.

### ✅ the PORTAL question is CLOSED — for the case that matters

> 🚩 **this section read "what remains genuinely open is whether the portal
> exposes an amended report for a year the charter was void" until a later pass.**
> the Division answered it **on the record** — and the reply predated the
> sentence that called it open.

a Franchise Tax analyst at the Division, by email, directed the filer to the
portal **while the charter stood void**:

> "Once receives you may **go online and file an amended 2022 report** to list
> the verified assets and issued shares. Then, once filed proceed with **filing
> an amended 2023 report** with the correct total issued shares.
>
> After all taxes are paid you can file a Certificate of Renewal."
>
> — Delaware Division of Corporations, Franchise Tax, by email (date withheld)

> 🚩 **the source bytes for that quotation do NOT ship, and that is a DECLARED
> PERMANENT GAP.** the email is held as a comms yield inside a matter directory
> that `.gitignore` excludes (`**/.demo/*`), because it carries a real entity, a
> real file number and a real person. ⇒ a `quote.verify` census aimed at the
> published sources alone reports this passage as **NOT-IN-SOURCE**.
>
> ⛔ that is an **ABSENT-SOURCE** verdict, never a fabrication verdict, and the
> two are indistinguishable from the count alone. do not widen the detector, and
> do not delete the quotation to make a number green. add your own matter
> directory to `--from` if you hold one, or read the gap as declared right here.

> ⛔ **so this template has TWO censuses, and a number is meaningless without the
> invocation beside it.** record both, always:
>
> | invocation | result |
> |---|---|
> | `--from …/refs --in templates` | `verified 138 · live 2` — the 2 are **this quote's two sentences**, expected |
> | `--from …/refs --from …/.demo/<matter> --in templates` | ✅ `verified 140 · live 0` |
>
> 🚩 **a remembered number from an unrecorded invocation cost three wrong
> predictions in two cycles.** each time the change was sound and the *comparator*
> came from a different instrument — which looks exactly like a broken change and
> says not one word about it. ⇒ **a baseline is a number AND the command that
> produced it.** carry them together or discard both.
>
> ⭐ **the free discriminator settles which case you are in, at zero cost:** if the
> defect list **equals** the set of gaps the page already declares, it is a
> `--from` omission — a fabrication cannot know what your source set contains.

> ⛔ **"2022" and "2023" are the QUOTED MATTER's years, not yours.** they stay
> because a quotation is verbatim or it is worthless (`rule.forbid.hand-transcription`)
> — a template may not swap a year inside quotation marks for a placeholder.
>
> 🚩 **"Once receives" is the analyst's own slip, and it stays too — corrected
> back to verbatim.** this passage carried `Once receive[d]` for weeks:
> a silent hand-repair of a verb, inside quotation marks, **nine lines above the
> sentence that forbids exactly that.** the year rule was honored and the verb
> rule was not, from one keystroke of tidiness.
>
> ⭐ **a principle a file states is not thereby a principle the file obeys** — and
> the miss was invisible to any reader, because a repaired quote reads *better*
> than a faithful one. `quote.verify` is what caught it: the match broke at char
> 12 against the source bytes on disk.
>
> ⚠️ so read the quote for its **shape**, never its digits: *the earliest
> delinquent year carries assets **and** shares; each later year carries the
> correction that year needs; the revival certificate comes **after** the money.*
> substitute your own delinquent years into that shape, and confirm the per-year
> content with the Division — the years a filer owes are set by § 510's trigger
> date for **that** charter, and no two matters share them.

> ⚠️ **"Certificate of Renewal" is her name for it; the statute is § 312, NOT
> § 314.** the office, the fee schedule and the form use *renewal* and *revival*
> for one instrument, so do not hunt for a separate "renewal" document — and do
> not follow the word into § 314, which is captioned *"Status of corporation"*
> and prescribes no procedure at all.
>
> ⇒ on the call, name the branch the way the catalogue does: **Corporation →
> Revival for Void**. the full trap, its three baits, and why **§ 311** is the
> costlier wrong door are worked in `4.file.revival.stone` under `## form`.

> 🚩 **TESTIMONY, not a publication — so it has no source bytes and never will.**
> `quote.verify` reports it as unverified against `refs/`, and that report is
> **correct**: there is no public document to compare it to.
>
> ⭐ **its artifact of record is the `grain=final` comms yield** that captured
> the reply verbatim on the day it arrived, per `rule.require.permanent-yields`.
> that yield is where a reader checks this quotation. it is deliberately **not**
> wired in as a `--from` here, because a route's own yield corroborates our
> bookkeeping rather than a publisher — and to point at it would turn the count
> green on the wrong evidence.
>
> ⚠️ **so weigh it as what it is.** an analyst's email is a **direction**, not
> law. every statutory claim in this route verifies against embedded bytes; this
> one rests on a named agency, a dated channel, and a preserved reply. that is
> strong enough to act on and too weak to override § 502 or § 312 — which is
> exactly why the table below splits what it settles from what it leaves open.

⭐ **so a void charter does not close the portal to back-year amendments.** the
statutory election under § 502(c) has an operational path, and it is self-serve.

### ⛔ but read WHICH cell that answers

two questions were fused into one sentence, and only one is now settled:

| the question | status |
|---|---|
| may you file an amended back-year report **while the charter is void**? | ✅ **yes** — directed by the Division, on the record |
| will the portal expose an amended report for a **tax year whose charter stood void**? | 🚩 **still open** — the years she named both predate the void |

⚠️ the distinction is not academic. the § 312(g) revival payment is capped at
what was due *"at the time its certificate of incorporation became forfeited or
void,"* so the years inside the void window sit outside that cap and are reached
by a different rule. **do not read a direction about pre-void years as coverage
of the void years.**
>
> ⭐ the call still earns its place — it is the cheapest way to learn the years,
> the balance, and whether each year takes an amended or an original report. it
> is a step, not the cure.

⛔ **do not pay from this call.** see the precondition at the head of
`3.pay.taxes.stone`: a payment made before the reports discharges the
Authorized-Shares number.

